/-!
# Differences of the Bose–Chowla set and the subgroup of order `g`

Let `K` be a finite field with `q ^ 2` elements and `θ` a generator of `Kˣ`, a primitive
`(q ^ 2 - 1)`-th root of unity. The Bose–Chowla set is
`B_q = {a ∈ ℤ/(q ^ 2 - 1) : θ ^ a - θ ∈ 𝔽_q}`, where `𝔽_q = {x ∈ K : x ^ q = x}` is the subfield
with `q` elements. If `g ∣ q - 1` and `H` is the subgroup of order `g` of `ℤ/(q ^ 2 - 1)`, generated
by `(q ^ 2 - 1) / g`, then `(B_q - B_q) ∩ H = {0}`: two elements of `B_q` that differ by an element
of `H` are equal. Schmutz and Tait use this to show that `B_q` maps injectively to the quotient of
`ℤ/(q ^ 2 - 1)` by `H`, in their construction of large sets of integers whose nonzero differences
are each represented at most `g` times.

## Proof

Let `a, b ∈ B_q` with `b ≤ a` and `a - b = k (q ^ 2 - 1) / g`, and put `ζ = θ ^ (a - b)`. Then
`ζ ^ g = θ ^ (k (q ^ 2 - 1)) = 1`, so `ζ ^ (q - 1) = 1` since `g ∣ q - 1`, and `ζ ∈ 𝔽_q`. Write
`θ ^ a = θ + c` and `θ ^ b = θ + d` with `c, d ∈ 𝔽_q`. From `θ ^ a = ζ θ ^ b` we get
`(1 - ζ) θ = ζ d - c`. The map `x ↦ x ^ q` is a ring endomorphism of `K`, since `q` is a power of
the characteristic, and it fixes `ζ`, `c` and `d`, so `(1 - ζ) θ ^ q = (1 - ζ) θ`. If `ζ ≠ 1`, this
gives `θ ^ (q - 1) = 1`, which is impossible because `θ` has order `q ^ 2 - 1 > q - 1`. Hence
`ζ = 1`, so `θ ^ a = θ ^ b` and `a = b`, both being smaller than the order of `θ`.

The arXiv version of the source (Eric Schmutz and Michael Tait, *Cardinalities of $g$-difference
sets*, arXiv:2501.11736v1, Section 4.2, Lemma 8) quotes this fact from the literature without
proof. It prints the conclusion as `(A - A) ∩ H = {0}`, but the proof of its Proposition 2 applies
it to two elements of `B_q`, which is the form proved here. The proof above is self-contained.

## Main results

* `MetaMathlibExt.boseChowla_sub_mem_subgroup_eq`: two elements `a, b < q ^ 2 - 1` of the
  Bose–Chowla set with `(q ^ 2 - 1) / g ∣ a - b` are equal.
-/

public section

namespace MetaMathlibExt

namespace boseChowla_sub_mem_subgroup_eq

/-- In a finite field with `q ^ 2` elements, `q` is a power of the characteristic, so the map
`x ↦ x ^ q` commutes with subtraction. -/
private theorem sub_pow_of_card_eq_sq {K : Type*} [Field K] [Finite K] {q : ℕ}
    (hK : Nat.card K = q ^ 2) (x y : K) : (x - y) ^ q = x ^ q - y ^ q := by
  have := Fintype.ofFinite K
  obtain ⟨n, hp, hcard⟩ := FiniteField.card K (ringChar K)
  have := Fact.mk hp
  rw [← Nat.card_eq_fintype_card, hK] at hcard
  obtain ⟨i, -, rfl⟩ := (Nat.dvd_prime_pow hp).1 (hcard ▸ dvd_pow_self q two_ne_zero)
  exact sub_pow_char_pow x y i

end boseChowla_sub_mem_subgroup_eq

open boseChowla_sub_mem_subgroup_eq in
/-- **Nonzero differences of the Bose–Chowla set avoid the subgroup of order $g$.** Let $q$
and $g$ be natural numbers with $g \mid q - 1$, let $K$ be a finite field with $q^2$ elements, and
let $\theta \in K$ be a primitive $(q^2 - 1)$-th root of unity, that is, a generator of $K^\times$.
If $a$ and $b$ are natural numbers less than $q^2 - 1$ with
$(\theta^a - \theta)^q = \theta^a - \theta$ and $(\theta^b - \theta)^q = \theta^b - \theta$, and
$(q^2 - 1)/g$ divides $a - b$, then $a = b$.

Equivalently, let $\mathbb{F}_q = \{x \in K : x^q = x\}$, let
$B_q = \{a \in \mathbb{Z}/(q^2 - 1) : \theta^a - \theta \in \mathbb{F}_q\}$ be the Bose–Chowla set
and let $H$ be the subgroup of $\mathbb{Z}/(q^2 - 1)$ generated by $(q^2 - 1)/g$; then
$(B_q - B_q) \cap H = \{0\}$.

Source: Eric Schmutz and Michael Tait, *Cardinalities of g-Difference Sets*, INTEGERS 25
(2025), Article A77, Lemma 9 (`integers-2025-A77-lem-9`), quoting Bose–Chowla and
Brandão–Debarre–Tait / Gómez–Trujillo–Tait. -/
theorem boseChowla_sub_mem_subgroup_eq {K : Type*} [Field K] [Finite K]
    (q g : ℕ) (hK : Nat.card K = q ^ 2) (hgq : g ∣ q - 1) (θ : K)
    (hθ : IsPrimitiveRoot θ (q ^ 2 - 1)) (a b : ℕ) (ha : a < q ^ 2 - 1) (hb : b < q ^ 2 - 1)
    (hBa : (θ ^ a - θ) ^ q = θ ^ a - θ) (hBb : (θ ^ b - θ) ^ q = θ ^ b - θ)
    (hab : (((q ^ 2 - 1) / g : ℕ) : ℤ) ∣ (a : ℤ) - b) :
    a = b := by
  -- The statement is symmetric in `a` and `b`.
  wlog hba : b ≤ a generalizing a b
  · exact (this b a hb ha hBb hBa (by rwa [← dvd_neg, neg_sub]) (by omega)).symm
  -- A field has at least two elements, so `q ≥ 2`.
  have hq : 2 ≤ q := by
    have h : 1 < q ^ 2 := hK ▸ Finite.one_lt_card
    by_contra! hq
    interval_cases q <;> simp at h
  have hqq : q < q ^ 2 := by nlinarith
  -- `ζ = θ ^ (a - b)` is a `g`-th root of unity, hence it lies in `𝔽_q`.
  obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ : (q ^ 2 - 1) / g ∣ a - b := by
    rwa [← Int.natCast_dvd_natCast, Nat.cast_sub hba]
  have hg : g ∣ q ^ 2 - 1 := hgq.trans (by simpa using Nat.sub_dvd_pow_sub_pow q 1 2)
  set ζ := θ ^ (a - b) with hζ
  have hζg : ζ ^ g = 1 := by
    rw [← pow_mul, hk, mul_right_comm, Nat.div_mul_cancel hg, pow_mul, hθ.pow_eq_one, one_pow]
  have hζq : ζ ^ q = ζ := by
    obtain ⟨j, hj⟩ := hgq
    rw [← Nat.sub_add_cancel (by omega : 1 ≤ q), pow_succ, hj, pow_mul, hζg, one_pow, one_mul]
  -- `(1 - ζ) θ = ζ (θ ^ b - θ) - (θ ^ a - θ)` is fixed by `x ↦ x ^ q`, and so is `ζ`.
  have hθa : θ ^ a = ζ * θ ^ b := by rw [hζ, ← pow_add, Nat.sub_add_cancel hba]
  have hkey : (1 - ζ) * θ = ζ * (θ ^ b - θ) - (θ ^ a - θ) := by rw [hθa]; ring
  have hfix : (1 - ζ) * θ ^ q = (1 - ζ) * θ := by
    have h := congrArg (· ^ q) hkey
    rwa [mul_pow, sub_pow_of_card_eq_sq hK, one_pow, hζq, sub_pow_of_card_eq_sq hK, mul_pow, hζq,
      hBa, hBb, ← hkey] at h
  -- If `ζ ≠ 1`, then `θ ∈ 𝔽_q`, impossible since `θ` has order `q ^ 2 - 1 > q - 1`.
  have hζ1 : ζ = 1 := by
    by_contra hne
    have hθq : θ ^ q = θ := mul_left_cancel₀ (sub_ne_zero.mpr (Ne.symm hne)) hfix
    refine hθ.pow_ne_one_of_pos_of_lt (l := q - 1) (by omega) (by omega) ?_
    refine mul_right_cancel₀ (hθ.ne_zero (by omega)) ?_
    rw [← pow_succ, Nat.sub_add_cancel (by omega), hθq, one_mul]
  exact hθ.pow_inj ha hb (by rw [hθa, hζ1, one_mul])

end MetaMathlibExt
